-- title:
--   There are fourteen cusp double cosets for $Γ_H(25)$
-- statement:
--   Let $Γ=Γ_H(25)≤SL_2(ℤ)$, let $T$ be translation, and let $⟨T,-I⟩$ be the subgroup generated by $T$ and the central matrix $-I$. Then $$|Γ\backslash SL_2(ℤ)/⟨T,-I⟩|=14.$$ This gives the number of geometric cusp orbits of the level-$25$ subgroup.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

